  "comment": "Two-node relay scenario mirroring a real production deployment: the entry node exposes one service per rule (all referencing one chain), the exit node runs a SINGLE relay listener for the whole tunnel — the relay protocol carries each connection's destination in-band, so N entry rules share one exit port, and that port is independent of (and may even numerically equal) the entry listen ports, which live on different machines. ingress_display_address on the tunnel is the address the entry dials for the relay handoff.",
